Z||000009||b_b_a_d||02-22-2000||04:11 AM||||I bought my wife an 85 Camaro w/Ttops.  She claimed the car as hers and now has plans to convert it to a superstock class race car.<P>I bought an 86 SE V6 Auto/Trans for myself and here is the new wife policy.  She is planning on tearing down the camaro and decided the fiero will be her car.  <BR> <BR>Every time I spent money on the car, the wife got upset... But now She fights to drive it every chance she gets!  This leaves me with the 94 voyager minivan.  It is a cool little sporty white van with tinted windows and a thumpin stereo, but in no way does this compare to the fiero guys!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000010||FIEROCIOUS||02-22-2000||04:56 AM||||My wife never complains, (an occational frown) maybe. She knows its my hobby and she accepts it as a part of who I am! She has allways been great! I love that girl!<P>Heres a tip: Say you want part X, it cost 100.00, but tell her it's 300.00 and you got a deal on it for a 100.00! (women love bargains)! Then take her to the store while it's still in her head that you bought a (stupid car part) and let her buy the useless crap that women like for half the price of your (stupid car part).<BR>Then (you all are not gonna like this) spend an hour letting her talk about useless stuff that women talk about. You get the part, she gets useless crap and attention! And life is good! An hour of time listening is better than years of crabbin and complaining!<P>Disclaimer: Result may vary. This is not a garantee. Void where prohibited.<P>P.S. How many doiles and candles do you need anyway? ||||reg||1
Z||000011||sdm1964||02-22-2000||08:42 AM||||It took years of going back and forth but she has realized that we will always have one more car in the driveway than we can drive. it might be in peices in the yard or in the garage as long as it is not in the house. This is who i am and i am a caraholic!!!! I don't skimp on bills to get parts, pay for all my toys with my own side job money, National guard check. The bathroom is pink but i will not sleep on pink sheets. ps any harrasment from this post will be dealt with in death. I am all man, thats what the wife tells me anyway. Yes dear i will get the trash in a sec. rub your back no prob. We both know how is the boss, SHE is.||||reg||14
Z||000012||turbo86se||02-22-2000||10:22 AM||||I really hate to rub it in, but I've yet to deal with the "wife!" Guess it's a good thing I'm single! I'll be 25 next month! The girl I'm dating now likes my Fieros, but doesn't understand my obsession. She's driven my 88 coupe, and liked it. She thinks I'm crazy because I very selectively drive my Turbo 86 SE, and because it's garage kept under a car cover! What's wrong with that? I have to look after my baby!  <BR>Speaking of selective driving, my neighbor in MD, before I moved to Myrtle, bought a red 88GT brand-new way back in 88. He got every option, maybe T-Tops, I can't remember. He knew it would be a collector. Anyways, he never drove it in rain, snow, if the sun's UV rays were above a 5. For his son's homecoming dance in high school, he let his son drive the Fiero and his date to dinner and the dance. It rained like he!! that night. His wife nearly had to sedate him, she thought he was going to have a heart attack  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  He even drove to the school, waiting in the parking lot for his son and the Fiero to pull in, so he could switch cars! <BR>I didn't see the GT much, but sometimes I saw him drive by in it, and it was the coolest car I've ever seen, not to mention how that V6 growled. I bet he's got no more than 5,000 miles on it now. <BR>The end of March I'm going back to MD for a visit, I'll definitely have to post some pics of it! ||||reg||10
Z||000013||Capt Fiero||02-22-2000||12:37 PM||||I guess I am really lucky, my girlfriend that I have been with and live with for 2 years now, loves Fiero's, loves my car, helps me work on it, even goes to the parts store and picks up parts for me.  She really wants a V-6 Auto for herself.  I showed her a 4cyl auto and that is what made here madd. She told me that if I thought that I was going to have my 6 and she was going to have a 4 I was nuts. ||||reg||10
